null,"result":"I approve PKT-0054. It answers the question it was given: the time goes to measuring each cell's text, mostly font shaping, plus number formatting and drawing; page setup is only about 3%. The executor backed this with a V8 CPU profile and experiments on test files, and kept wall time out of the comparison because the shared VM made it unreliable.\n\n**Why it passes the rejection rules**\n- The executor log is filled in, with decisions, surprises and what was not done.\n- The requested follow-up is listed both under \"Spawned packets\" and in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- This is an investigate packet, not a characterize one, so the rule about keeping surprises in tests doesn't apply.\n- The contract is respected: nothing outside `.theseus/` changed and sdkjs was not touched.\n- The friction line was added.\n\n**Weaknesses, none serious enough to reject**\n1. **Budget:** the diff touches 7 files and the packet allows 6. The extra ones are the packet's own bookkeeping (the friction line and the spawn request), so I don't count it against the work.\n2. **Weak page-setup test:** the fit-to-width variant uses only 8 columns, which already fit one page wide, so it could never show a difference. The \"page setup is not the cause\" conclusion rests on the 3% share of `calcPagesPrint` in the profile, not on this experiment. The diagnosis says as much.\n3. **Rows that can't be regenerated:** the 6,250- and 12,500-row results in the table can't be rebuilt with `xlsx-variants.py`, which only makes the 25k and 50k sizes. The linear-scaling claim still holds on the 25k and 50k points.\n4. **Script comment:** `xlsx-variants.py` says to run `x2t-split.sh` on its output files, but the CPU numbers came from `x2t-cpu.sh`.\n5. **Single runs:** each variant was measured once. That's acceptable since CPU time varied by about 5%, and the executor says so.\n6. **Profiler tool:** `x2t-cpuprofile.js` assumes the global `WebSocket` available in recent Node versions and has no fallback if the inspector port is busy. That's fine for a diagnostic tool.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Goal answered with profile evidence (text shaping and formatting ~79%, drawing ~33%, page setup ~3%); log, spawned follow-up and friction present; minor gaps in reproducibility and the fit test","ttft_ms":2261,"type":"result","duration_ms":15292,"uuid":"7400aa9e-7035-4586-a335-127a36622a68","ttft_stream_ms":904,"time_to_request_ms":355,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":191,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":10,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":32,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":7,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":64,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":205,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_peak_rss_mib":254,"process_cpu_ms_turn":979,"process_wall_ms_turn":15291,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":387,"process_wall_ms_streaming":12246,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":234,"main_stream_chunk_count":61,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":12,"cpu_ms":23,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":11,"render_ms":4,"producers":41,"token_counts":0},"first_content_frame_ms":905,"time_to_request_from_spawn_ms":19492433,"warm_spare_claimed":false,"flag_fetch_kick":"started_in_init_warm","time_origin_ms":1793654948982.3232,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"process_start_tuning":0}
